package m07core029run
    provides [checks, expected_vector, observe, case_body, descriptor, context, check, check_ref, expected_check, evidence, observation, failed, test_case]
    uses [text]

/// M07 CORE-029 "bundled Noul judge: production run shape".
/// Source: tests/integration/judge_test.go symbol
/// TestCurrentBundledNoulJudge.
/// Related fixture: compiler/testdata/current/native/noul.can main entry
/// (L53-71); the live run helper (L74-91) executes the sandboxed binary
/// under the combined profile with a localhost-only allowance, and the
/// raw-provider leg builds the auth-stripped program (L137-164) and drives
/// the compiled main through a bun harness (L166-202).
/// Disposition: RETAIN (migrate row; the old Go harness stays until the
/// integrator retires it after every linked row, variant, environment and
/// control has accepted evidence).
/// Protects (this file): the production process shape. The green run exits
/// 0 with stdout "TFT" and empty stderr; the assert leg exits 0 with empty
/// stderr and a report carrying supplied-completion; the sandbox profile
/// and the credential env plumbing pin the invocation contract; the
/// raw-provider build exits 0 with a directory carrying the compiled main
/// import and exactly one runtime; the bun harness run exits 0 under the
/// deny-network profile with the empty snapshot file. Unlike silent-entry
/// rows, the run stdout is pinned verbatim (adaptation below, CORE-014
/// precedent).
/// The 3-root green pin lives in core-029-roots-green.can; live judge
/// semantics live in core-029-judge-semantics.can.
/// Variants: none live in this file beyond the green run, assert, build
/// and harness legs themselves; the invalid/blank/faulty rejections and
/// the raw-provider assertion semantics belong to the judge-semantics
/// file.
/// Adaptation: the Go test pins the green run stdout with full equality
/// (L92: out must be exactly "TFT", the T/F/T markers the three
/// likelihood relays write via report), so "TFT" is pinned verbatim here
/// as run-stdout per the accepted CORE-014/019/040 non-silent-output
/// precedent. The assert stdout is pinned by substring containment (L95:
/// out contains "supplied-completion"), so the verbatim needle is pinned
/// as assert-stdout-label, not the whole report.
/// Environment: CAN_BUN_ARCHIVE + macOS sandbox-exec; requires
/// can-bun-archive, macos-sandbox-exec. CAN_I17_TOKEN is harness-supplied
/// (Go L79: "test-only"), not an external gate. Logical gates SUITE/DIAG/
/// FAULT and C/R/N/S/A identities bind at P23/QHTTP; no live run now.
/// Descriptor timeout 120000ms mirrors the Go 2-minute ctx (L27).
/// Delegated oracles: none.
/// Execution credit: NOT claimed (accept_after P23/QHTTP unmet).
/// Case bundled/judge-run checks: run-exit, run-stdout, run-stderr-empty,
/// assert-exit, assert-stderr-empty, assert-stdout-label, sandbox-profile,
/// credential-env, build-exit, build-directory, main-import, runtime-single,
/// harness-exit, harness-snapshot, harness-profile.
/// Facet map (judge_test.go legs): run-exit pins exit 0 on the green run
/// (L92-94: status 0 or "judge execution" fatals); run-stdout pins the
/// non-silent stdout verbatim (L92: out must be exactly "TFT");
/// run-stderr-empty pins empty stderr on the green run (L92: diag must be
/// ""); assert-exit pins exit 0 on the assert leg (L95-97: status 0 or
/// "ordinary Noul consumer assertions" fatals); assert-stderr-empty pins
/// empty stderr on the assert leg (L95: diag must be "");
/// assert-stdout-label pins the non-silent assert stdout (L95: out
/// contains "supplied-completion"; needle pinned, not the whole report);
/// sandbox-profile pins the combined run profile verbatim (L76: "(version
/// 1)(allow default)(deny network*)(allow network-outbound (remote ip
/// "localhost:*"))"); credential-env pins the credential plumbing (L79:
/// CAN_I17_TOKEN=test-only in the run environment); build-exit pins exit 0
/// on the raw-provider build (L143-146: status 0 or "raw-provider build"
/// fatals); build-directory pins the JSON directory (L147-152: stdout
/// unmarshals to a directory); main-import pins the compiled main import
/// (L157-160: entry.ts matches the $canFunction import as $canMain, the
/// stable "as $canMain" fragment pinned); runtime-single pins the runtime
/// count (L161-164: exactly 1 runtime/r-* glob hit or "missing shared
/// runtime" fatals); harness-exit pins exit 0 on the bun harness run
/// (L198-201: CombinedOutput error or "compiled raw provider assertion"
/// fatals); harness-snapshot pins the fd snapshot (L186-187:
/// environment.json holds "{}"; L197: passed as the extra file);
/// harness-profile pins the deny-network harness profile verbatim (L195:
/// "(version 1)(allow default)(deny network*)").
/// Shared old files untouched; retirement is a later integrator decision.
